{"text": "RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT, NEUCHATEL - QUARTERLY REPORT\n\nDIVISTON\n\nRESEARCH\n\nSUBJECT TITLE\n\nHYDRA-ETS\nPERIOD COVERED : APRIL ~ JUNE 1989\nWRITTEN BY 1 Gerber-c. (CAG)\n\nKEYWORDS : epoleon, ets, volatile-organic-compounds\n\nPROJECT HYDRA\n\nobjective\n\nobtain an analytical data-base on ETS through indoor air\nmonitoring experiments.\n\nstatus\n\n\u2018The determination of benzene, toluene and isoprene concentration\nin indoor air was tested in real-life situations by sampling in\noffices within the R&D building, with or without smoking in the\nroom. The procedure is based on'the thermal desorbtion technique\nwith tenax as a trapping agent [1]. Peak identity was confirmed\nby GC-MS.\nIn spite of the high background of solvent vapours (laboratories\nin the building), the method gave satisfactory results for the\nquantification of toluene; for benzene, the background levels\nwere often higher than the ETS contribution, making the\nquantification dubious. The agreement between replicates was\ngood for both determinations and the sensitivity adequate.\nThe isoprene results were erratic. The problem was traced to a\npoor retention of the compound by the preconcentration trap.\n\nPROJECT ETS\n\nObjectives\n\nSupport S&T in the organization of sub-contracted studies on ETS.\n\nTest analytical procedures through collaborative studies with\nexternal laboratories.\nRespond to PME requests for studies implicating real-life\nanalyses in ETS.\n\nstatus\n\nThe collaborative study with Battelle (1]| was finalized. Sone\ntechnical recommendations have been made in to order to improve\nthe reproducibility of their results [2].\n\nSZ0SE98z0z",
